# Which came first?
subtitle: "The fax or the telephone? Oxford or the Aztecs? The pyramids or the last mammoths? Tap the older one, and watch history's timeline fold."

## Which came first?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: bain
      title: Alexander Bain (inventor)
      authors: Wikipedia
      year: 2025
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Bain_(inventor)
      finding: Bain received British patent 9745 for his 'electric printing telegraph', the first fax, on 27 May 1843; Bell's telephone patent came in 1876
    - id: oxford
      title: 'University of Oxford: history'
      authors: University of Oxford
      year: 2024
      finding: there is no clear date of foundation, but teaching existed at Oxford in some form in 1096
    - id: wrangel
      title: Temporal dynamics of woolly mammoth genome erosion prior to extinction (Cell)
      authors: M. Dehasque et al.
      year: 2024
      finding: the Wrangel Island mammoth population survived until about 4,000 years ago

    cards pairs cites ["bain","oxford","wrangel"] size 1 unit "years ago" compare "Tap the older one" hidden true
        * "Fax machine" icon "fax machine" value 183
        * "Telephone" icon telephone value 150
        * "Tenochtitlan" icon.of "hindu temple" icon.or ["lake"] icon.set twemoji value 701
        * "Oxford lectures" icon "graduation cap" value 930
        * "Last mammoth" icon mammoth value 4000
        * "Great Pyramid" icon ["pyramid","desert"] value 4580
    text vs1 "vs" right pairs_1 gap 14 #8f887c font_size 30 hidden true
    text vs3 "vs" right pairs_3 gap 14 #8f887c font_size 30 hidden true
    text vs5 "vs" right pairs_5 gap 14 #8f887c font_size 30 hidden true
    text c_pend "2 pendulums" left pairs_1 gap 16 #b5482e font_size 26 hidden true
    text c_lake "on a lake" left pairs_3 gap 16 #b5482e font_size 26 hidden true
    text c_bc "2560 BC" right pairs_6 gap 16 #b5482e font_size 26 hidden true
    text c_wr "Wrangel Is." left pairs_5 gap 16 #b5482e font_size 26 hidden true

    card title "Which came first?"

Which came first? Three pairs, and in each one, history plays a trick on you.
    draw pairs vs1 vs3 vs5

    ask "Which came first? In each pair, tap the one that is older." on pairs store c feedback.style warm feedback.perfect "A historian's instinct." feedback.good "History tricked you only a little." feedback.poor "These three fool almost everyone." feedback.none "History won this round."
        right: The fax, Oxford and the pyramid all came first.
        wrong: {c.within} of {c.total} on the first try.

Start with the fax.
    highlight pairs_1

Alexander Bain patented a way to send pictures by telegraph in 1843, thirty-three years before Bell's phone.
    highlight pairs_v_1

His design used two swinging pendulums, kept in step, to scan a picture line by line.
    draw c_pend

Next, Oxford was teaching students by 1096, more than two centuries before the Aztecs founded their capital, Tenochtitlan.
    text c_1096 "by 1096" right pairs_4 gap 16 #b5482e font_size 26

So when that city rose from its lake, Oxford had already been teaching for generations.
    draw c_lake

And the Great Pyramid is older than the last woolly mammoths.
    highlight pairs_6

The pyramid was finished around 2560 BC.
    draw c_bc

A small herd survived on Wrangel Island, in the Arctic Ocean, until about four thousand years ago.
    draw c_wr

So when the pyramid was already five centuries old, mammoths still walked the Earth.
    highlight pairs_5 pairs_v_5 pairs_6 pairs_v_6
